{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.QBetaZeta4ResidueRefutation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.QBetaZeta4ResidueRefutation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":27,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Zeta4Residue.disc_shared_prime_19","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Zeta4Residue.disc_shared_prime_19","kind":"theorem","line":286,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/QBetaZeta4ResidueRefutation.lean#L286-L292","doc":"**Shared prime `19`.** `−152 = −(2³·19)` and `−76 = −(2²·19)`: the two\nsector discriminants differ by a factor of `2` and share the prime `19` —\nthe arithmetic fingerprint recorded in the 2026-07-07 audit, now\ncertified over `ℤ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Zeta4Residue.cubicC_Hopf_disc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Zeta4Residue.cubicC_Hopf_disc","kind":"theorem","line":281,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/QBetaZeta4ResidueRefutation.lean#L281-L284","doc":"**`disc C_Hopf = −76`.** With the `cubicC_Hopf_coeffs` reading, the\ndiscriminant of the Hopf-sector cubic evaluates exactly. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Zeta4Residue.cubicC_disc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Zeta4Residue.cubicC_disc","kind":"theorem","line":276,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/QBetaZeta4ResidueRefutation.lean#L276-L279","doc":"**`disc C = −152`.** With the `cubicC_coeffs` reading, the discriminant\nof the total carrier cubic evaluates exactly. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Zeta4Residue.cubicC_Hopf_coeffs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Zeta4Residue.cubicC_Hopf_coeffs","kind":"theorem","line":271,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/QBetaZeta4ResidueRefutation.lean#L271-L274","doc":"Coefficient reading of the Hopf-sector cubic: `(p, q, r) = (−6, 10, −6)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Zeta4Residue.cubicC_coeffs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Zeta4Residue.cubicC_coeffs","kind":"theorem","line":265,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/QBetaZeta4ResidueRefutation.lean#L265-L269","doc":"Coefficient reading of the total carrier cubic: `C = y³ − 4y² + 3y − 2`\nis monic with `(p, q, r) = (−4, 3, −2)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Zeta4Residue.cubicDisc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Zeta4Residue.cubicDisc","kind":"def","line":261,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/QBetaZeta4ResidueRefutation.lean#L261-L263","doc":"Discriminant of a monic cubic `y³ + p·y² + q·y + r`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Zeta4Residue.cubicC_unknot_classical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Zeta4Residue.cubicC_unknot_classical","kind":"theorem","line":244,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/QBetaZeta4ResidueRefutation.lean#L244-L249","doc":"**Unknot-sector value at the classical point.** `C_unknot(2) = −2` — the\nidentity sector coincidentally also equals `−2` at `y = 2`; recorded so the\nshadow match is not mis-read as Hopf-exclusive. The total is\n`C(2) = C_Hopf(2) + C_unknot(2) = −4` (`cubicC_two`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Zeta4Residue.cubicC_Hopf_classical_shadow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Zeta4Residue.cubicC_Hopf_classical_shadow","kind":"theorem","line":238,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/QBetaZeta4ResidueRefutation.lean#L238-L242","doc":"**Shadow identity.** `C_Hopf(2) = −2` — the Hopf-sector cubic at the\nclassical trace value `y = 2` (`q = 1`) equals the c_3 q=1 shadow\n`−2 = J_Hopf(1)` (KC10). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Zeta4Residue.cubicC_Hopf_rrt_candidates_all_nonzero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Zeta4Residue.cubicC_Hopf_rrt_candidates_all_nonzero","kind":"theorem","line":211,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/QBetaZeta4ResidueRefutation.lean#L211-L220","doc":"**The Hopf-sector cubic has no rational root** (RRT candidates = divisors of\n`6`, i.e. `{±1, ±2, ±3, ±6}`, all nonzero: `C_Hopf` = `−1, −23, −2, −58, −3,\n−117, 54, −498`), so it is irreducible over `ℚ`: the double-crossing sector\nalone already carries an irreducible cubic field (disc `−76 = −2²·19`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Zeta4Residue.cubicC_sector_decomp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Zeta4Residue.cubicC_sector_decomp","kind":"theorem","line":203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/QBetaZeta4ResidueRefutation.lean#L203-L209","doc":"**Sector decomposition of the odd-channel cubic.** `C = C_Hopf + C_unknot`:\nthe total cubic splits exactly into the Hopf-sector cubic plus the\nunknot-sector quadratic. The `y³` term — hence the degree-3 field — lives\nentirely in the Hopf (double-crossing) summand. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Zeta4Residue.cubicC_Hopf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Zeta4Residue.cubicC_Hopf","kind":"def","line":199,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/QBetaZeta4ResidueRefutation.lean#L199-L201","doc":"Hopf/double-crossing-sector contribution: the **cubic** `C_Hopf(y) =\ny³ − 6y² + 10y − 6` — the source of the degree-3 field. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Zeta4Residue.cubicC_unknot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Zeta4Residue.cubicC_unknot","kind":"def","line":195,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/QBetaZeta4ResidueRefutation.lean#L195-L197","doc":"Unknot/identity-sector contribution to the odd-channel cubic: the quadratic\n`C_unknot(y) = 2y² − 7y + 4` (disc `17`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Zeta4Residue.cubicC_rrt_candidates_all_nonzero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Zeta4Residue.cubicC_rrt_candidates_all_nonzero","kind":"theorem","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/QBetaZeta4ResidueRefutation.lean#L159-L167","doc":"**No rational root (`ℚ`).** The four RRT candidates `{±1, ±2}` are the only\npossible rational roots of the monic integer cubic `C`; each is nonzero\n(`cubicC_one/neg_one/two/neg_two`), so `C` has no root in `ℚ` and is\nirreducible over `ℚ`. Stated as the disjunction of the certified\nnon-vanishings that the rational root theorem reduces the claim to. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Zeta4Residue.cubicC_silver","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Zeta4Residue.cubicC_silver","kind":"theorem","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/QBetaZeta4ResidueRefutation.lean#L155-L157","doc":"**Silver-anchor trace value `y = (1+√2)²+(1+√2)⁻² = 6`:** `C(6) = 88 ≠ 0` —\nthe silver substrate anchor is not a root of the odd-channel cubic. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Zeta4Residue.cubicC_golden","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Zeta4Residue.cubicC_golden","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/QBetaZeta4ResidueRefutation.lean#L151-L153","doc":"**Golden-anchor trace value `y = φ²+φ⁻² = 3`:** `C(3) = −2 ≠ 0` — the golden\nsubstrate anchor is not a root of the odd-channel cubic. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Zeta4Residue.cubicC_neg_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Zeta4Residue.cubicC_neg_two","kind":"theorem","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/QBetaZeta4ResidueRefutation.lean#L148-L149","doc":"**RRT candidate `y = −2`:** `C(−2) = −32 ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Zeta4Residue.cubicC_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Zeta4Residue.cubicC_two","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/QBetaZeta4ResidueRefutation.lean#L144-L146","doc":"**RRT candidate `y = 2` (also the classical `q = 1` trace value):**\n`C(2) = −4 ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Zeta4Residue.cubicC_neg_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Zeta4Residue.cubicC_neg_one","kind":"theorem","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/QBetaZeta4ResidueRefutation.lean#L141-L142","doc":"**RRT candidate `y = −1`:** `C(−1) = −10 ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Zeta4Residue.cubicC_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Zeta4Residue.cubicC_one","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/QBetaZeta4ResidueRefutation.lean#L138-L139","doc":"**RRT candidate `y = 1`:** `C(1) = −2 ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Zeta4Residue.R12_eq_cubic_trace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Zeta4Residue.R12_eq_cubic_trace","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/QBetaZeta4ResidueRefutation.lean#L110-L118","doc":"**Literal trace-cubic form (`Field`, `q ≠ 0`):** `R₁₂ = q⁶·C(q²+q⁻²)` with\nthe trace variable `y = q²+q⁻²` written explicitly. The `Field`/`q ≠ 0`\nhypothesis is only to admit `q⁻²`; the content is the division-free\n`R12_eq_trace_cubic_shift`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Zeta4Residue.R12_eq_trace_cubic_shift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Zeta4Residue.R12_eq_trace_cubic_shift","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/QBetaZeta4ResidueRefutation.lean#L98-L108","doc":"**Division-free trace-cubic form of `R₁₂`.** `R₁₂ = q⁶·C(q²+q⁻²)` with\n`C(y) = y³−4y²+3y−2`, written without inverses by clearing `q⁶`:\n`R₁₂ = (q⁴+1)³ − 4q²(q⁴+1)² + 3q⁴(q⁴+1) − 2q⁶` (each `q⁶·yᵏ` becomes a\ngenuine polynomial via `q²·(q²+q⁻²) = q⁴+1`). The odd carrier's surviving\ncontent is a **degree-3 object in the bar-even trace variable**, not a\ncyclotomic factor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Zeta4Residue.numOdd_at_phi4_root","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Zeta4Residue.numOdd_at_phi4_root","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/QBetaZeta4ResidueRefutation.lean#L86-L94","doc":"**`num` evaluates to the constant `−64` at every root of `Φ₄`** (e.g.\n`q = i` over `ℂ`, where `q²+1 = 0`). Hence `num` has no `Φ₄` factor: the\nscope-(b) exclusion of the ζ₄-residue route, cited invariant. (Over a ring\nwhere `(64 : R) ≠ 0` — e.g. `ℤ, ℚ, ℝ, ℂ` — this is a genuine non-vanishing;\nthe value `−64` itself holds over any `CommRing`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Zeta4Residue.numOdd_phi4_quot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Zeta4Residue.numOdd_phi4_quot","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/QBetaZeta4ResidueRefutation.lean#L75-L84","doc":"**Exact division of `num` by `Φ₄ = q²+1` leaves the nonzero constant\nremainder `−64`.** `num + 64 = (q²+1)·Q` with `Q` the explicit degree-12\nquotient. Since the remainder is a nonzero constant, `Φ₄ ∤ num`: the\nζ₄ = i **residue** is absent from the odd carrier. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Zeta4Residue.numOdd_factor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Zeta4Residue.numOdd_factor","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/QBetaZeta4ResidueRefutation.lean#L67-L71","doc":"**The only cyclotomic content of `num` is the trivial `q²−1`.**\n`num = (q²−1)·R₁₂` — the `Φ₁·Φ₂` factor, with the rest carried by the\nnon-cyclotomic palindromic `R₁₂`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Zeta4Residue.cubicC","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Zeta4Residue.cubicC","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/QBetaZeta4ResidueRefutation.lean#L62-L63","doc":"The surviving cubic in the bar-even trace variable: `C(y) = y³−4y²+3y−2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Zeta4Residue.R12","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Zeta4Residue.R12","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/QBetaZeta4ResidueRefutation.lean#L57-L60","doc":"The palindromic degree-12 cofactor `R₁₂` (the non-cyclotomic substance of\nthe odd carrier). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Zeta4Residue.numOdd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Zeta4Residue.numOdd","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/QBetaZeta4ResidueRefutation.lean#L51-L55","doc":"Numerator of the bar-odd part of the net decay-width carrier\n`Δ_odd(q) = num(q) / (4q⁷)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}